    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/migration-plan.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "0.3 — Decide what folio is",
      "prov:value": "From the [issue comment](https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/issues/223#issuecomment-5726628913):",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#223 comment"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/migration-plan.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Phase I — move code to the target shape, still one repo",
      "prov:value": "**I.1 takes two gates, and it took one until 2026-09-30.** The row above read\n*\"Gate the result: `bun run cat check:partition --strict` in CI\"*, which was the\nwhole gate — and `check:partition` resolves its `ROOT` to **one instance**, so\nevery `0 wrong-direction edges` it prints is scoped to that instance's own\nmodules and is silent about edges between the already-extracted siblings.\nI.1 was therefore discharged on one instance's evidence and reported as done.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/migration-plan.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Phase I — move code to the target shape, still one repo",
      "prov:value": "Bean `bf5l` measured the gap rather than arguing it. With a real\nwrong-direction import in place (`cat-harness/schemas/intake.ts` importing\n`folio-assistant-core`): `check:instance-graph` ✓ no cycle, `check:partition`\n**0**, `kg:detangle` **1**. Its own sentence — *\"three green checks did not mean\nthe layering held.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean bf5l"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/migration-plan.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Phase I — move code to the target shape, still one repo",
      "prov:value": "Bean `p11x`, owner's ruling of 2026-09-30 (**Option 2**): `check:partition`\nstays instance-scoped and `kg:detangle` owns the cross-instance axis, since it\nalready sees it. The alternative — widening `check:partition`'s root to the\ncheckout — was considered and rejected: its path rules are written against\ninstance-relative paths, so it would have meant reclassifying ~17 instances'\nmodules to reach a fact another tool already reports.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean p11x",
        "2026-09-30",
        "Option 2"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
